Line 1: I expected "as" here, but found "0.2".
    keep rate 0.2
              ^^^
Write it like "keep tax_rate as 0.2".

Line 2: "a" can't be used as a name.
    keep a as 1
         ^
EasyScript ignores the words "a", "an" and "the" wherever they appear, so they can't be names.
Try a name that says what it holds, like "total" or "answer".

Line 3: "yes" can't be used as a name.
    keep yes as 1
         ^^^
"yes" already means something in EasyScript.
Try a different name, like "my_yes".

Line 4: Something is missing after "as".
    keep rate as
              ^^
Add a value there, like a number, some text in quotes, or a name.

Line 5: I expected "keep doing this until" here, but found "doing this while".
    keep doing this while x:
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Write it like "keep doing this until done:".
